    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_b39ec4c5",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes a photo of actor John Malkovich with a photo of a man carrying a cross while being escorted by police, with the text \"some people say religion is a labor of love.\" The intent is to mock or ridicule the idea that religious devotion is noble or selfless, by contrasting it with the image of a man being physically restrained by authorities while carrying a cross, implying that religious practice can be burdensome or even dangerous. This framing can be seen as harmful as it potentially stigmatizes religious individuals or practices by suggesting they are inherently problematic or require coercion, which may contribute to negative perceptions of religion or religious people. The meme does not target any specific protected group with hate or abuse, but it does present a negative and potentially misleading portrayal of religious devotion, which can be harmful to religious communities or individuals who may feel misrepresented or attacked.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_a5d3d698"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
